CADCraft VAIO preview

Unofficial Xenial i386 adaptation; open CADCraft (VAIO preview) from Graphics or
VAIO App Launcher. The upstream CPU drawing path is presented with Glow on the
VAIO's software OpenGL, with a private package-local libxcb library. The drafting
engine, command line, constraints, formats and existing autosave are retained.

Use DXF working copies. Upstream is pre-alpha: saving DWG may discard unsupported
entities/data, and production/external-file fidelity is unverified. Many command
options, plotting and geometry operations remain incomplete; this is not a full
3D modeler or a claim of AutoCAD parity. Do not overwrite valuable originals.

Headless: cadcraft-vaio-cli --help
Example: cadcraft-vaio-cli convert Drawing.dxf Drawing.pdf
MCP: cadcraft-vaio-cli mcp
Desktop automation is opt-in with --control PORT, loopback only without auth.
Automation runs with the account's file access; use explicit disposable paths.
Normal launches start no control/MCP listener.

Autosave uses SAVETIME (upstream default 10 minutes) and SAVEFILEPATH, normally
~/.config/cadcraft/autosave. Drawing Recovery offers stopped sessions after the
lock lease expires (up to five minutes); opened copies need Save As. Profile and
workspace data stay under ~/.config/cadcraft unless CADCRAFT_CONFIG_DIR is set.

Seven hash-verified open native fallback fonts and their licences are included,
following upstream font exclusions; the original CADCraft Stroke font remains.
acadrust 0.6.4 is an unmodified MPL-2.0 library; see its licence/source notice.
APT manages installation and updates through the existing native frontend.
Remove with sudo apt-get remove cadcraft-vaio; user files/settings are retained.
